  "premise": "FICTIONAL ALTERNATE TIMELINE, June 2026. Ten days of crisis allowed precautionary deployments. A maritime confrontation escalated into reciprocal weapons fire overnight. NATO must preserve a supply ship and forward air operations against a limited Russian air-maritime attack off Latvia. No land invasion has begun. This is a bounded game force package, not a claim about actual deployments.",
  "blue_intent": "Preserve Baltic Sustainment 1 and both forward air bases. Defeat two strike aircraft and one forward corvette. Combine CAP, ship defenses and shore SAM cover. SEAD and precision-strike aircraft begin on hold for player tasking; attack only designated coastal threats when needed.",
  "red_intent": "Disrupt NATO sustainment and forward air operations with two maritime-strike and two land-strike aircraft, fighter cover and two forward corvettes. A frigate supports the naval force; coastal defenses protect the southern approaches.",
  "escalation_constraints": [
    "Conventional weapons only.",
    "NATO shore engagement is restricted by commander intent to Russian Coastal Battery, Russian Coastal Radar, Russian SAM Sector and Russian Point Defense. Briefing guidance is not an engine-enforced whitelist.",
    "Russian Air Base and civilian infrastructure are not NATO victory targets.",
    "Ground maneuver formations and occupation of Latvia or Estonia are outside this opening air-maritime battle."
  ],
